      "title": "Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Operations Coordinator | External Job Board Marian University Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Operations Coordinator Job Category : Admissions Requisition Number : OPERA001544 Apply now Posting Details Posted : September 4, 2026 Full-Time On-site Locations Showing 1 location Marian University 3200 Cold Spring Rd Indianapolis, IN 46222, USA Marian University 3200 Cold Spring Rd Indianapolis, IN 46222, USA +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description As a part of a diverse community of faculty and staff who represent many faith systems and worldviews, Marian University seeks an Operations Coordinator within Health Professions Admissions to promote our Catholic Franciscan mission and identity by supporting prospective students in their journey towards a career in the health professions. In this role you will play a vital role in supporting prospective students in their journey towards a career in the health professions. Your passion for education, operations, and data management will contribute to the continued success of our graduate health programs. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Actively engage the Catholic Franciscan mission and identity of Marian University by modeling the Franciscan Sponsorship Values and honoring the legacy of the founding congregation through transformative education, unity in diversity, leadership through service, integrating faith and life, and institutional policies. Coordinate day-to-day admissions operations for health professions programs ensuring smooth workflow and compliance with institutional policies. Serve as a central point of contact for prospective applicants regarding admissions processes, deadlines, and documentation. Manage admissions data entry and record-keeping, including maintaining accurate applicant files and updating databases or CRM systems. Support communications with applicants throughout the admissions lifecycle, from initial inquiry through enrollment decisions. Work closely with admissions counselors, program directors, administrative staff, and enrollment management to ensure alignment of processes and goals. Draft and send routine correspondence to applicants, departments, and external stakeholders. Utilize admissions software and CRM tools to track applicants, document interactions, and generate reports for leadership. Ensure compliance with university policies, FERPA, and relevant accreditation requirements in handling applicant data. Help analyze operational metrics (e.g., application trends, event attendance, conversion rates) to support process improvements. Identify areas for workflow efficiency, recommend enhancements, and assist in implementing updated procedures. Maintain and update admissions documentation, checklists, and process guide to reflect best practices and institutional changes. Support special projects or strategic initiatives aimed at improving health professions enrollment outcomes. University Expectations: Knowledge of and a commitment to the mission of Marian University Adheres to Marian University’s policies and procedures Shows courtesy and respect in interactions with fellow employees, students, subordinates, and supervisors Communicates regularly with supervisor about Department issues Meets department productivity standards Participates in developing department goals, objectives, and systems Assists to establish department measurements that align and support the accomplishment of the University’s strategic goals Adheres to the department budget Required Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Associate’s or Bachelor's degree in education, business, analytics, marketing, communications, or a related field. Over 10 years of relevant experience will be accepted in lieu of the degree. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For Consideration All Applications Require: Cover Letter Current resume or CV Contact information of three professional references.  The reference contact information must be entered after the application is submitted in the \"My Presence\" section of the applicant profile. Responses to the supplementary mission & identity questions. Please Review Marian University’s Mission & Identity Statement before responding to the supplementary questions on your application: https://www.marian.edu/faith Essential Functions: Highly desired: Previous experience working in a professional school admissions office. Demonstrated ability to write professional correspondence and effectively present information, responding to questions with clarity and professionalism. Proven track record of meeting deadlines for meetings, projects, reports, and assignments. Proficient computer skills, including a strong command of relevant software applications. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, enabling effective collaboration with diverse stakeholders. Physical Requirements: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit; use their hands to handle or feel objects, equipment, or controls; and talk or hear. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, reach with their hands and arms, climb or balance, and stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 50 pounds.  Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, and the ability to adjust focus. Work Environment: The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Limitations and Disclaimer: The above job description is meant to describe the general nature and level of work being performed; it is not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required for the position. All job requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities.  Some requirements may exclude individuals who pose a direct threat or significant risk to the health and safety of themselves or other employees. This job description in no way states or implies that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Employees will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and to perform other job-related duties requested by their supervisor in compliance with Federal and States Laws. Requirements are representative of minimum levels of knowledge, skills and/or abilities.  To perform this job successfully, the employee must possess the abilities or aptitudes to perform each duty proficiently.  Continued employment remains on an “at-will” basis. Marian University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All individuals, including minorities, women, individuals with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws. \nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. Success with Purpose You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://marian.rec.pro.ukg.net/MAR1500MNUI/JobBoard/fde73847-46d9-4c8a-924e-a28b5c630bfc/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=fb7c6987-1f92-4a82-96ba-95fa6ae5d94d": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor/Administrative Assistant- Nursing",
      "description": "Academic Advisor/Administrative Assistant- Nursing | External Job Board Marian University Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Academic Advisor/Administrative Assistant- Nursing Job Category : Academics Requisition Number : ACADE001541 Apply now Posting Details Posted : August 26, 2026 Full-Time On-site Locations Showing 1 location Plymouth 20097 9b Rd Plymouth, IN 46563, USA Plymouth 20097 9b Rd Plymouth, IN 46563, USA +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description As a part of a diverse community of faculty and staff who represent many faith systems and worldviews, Marian University seeks an Academic Advisor/Administrative Assistant for the Leighton School of Nursing (LSON) at the Plymouth Campus to promote our Catholic Franciscan mission and identity by supporting student success through academic advising, recruitment, retention, progression, and administrative excellence. This is a dual position in the Leighton School of Nursing (LSON) at Marian University Plymouth. Major responsibilities of the academic advisor role include academic advising and support, recruitment, retention, and progression of prospective and current nursing students. The advisor works collaboratively with faculty, professional staff, students, and other university personnel to support the admission, progression, and graduation of nursing students. Major responsibilities of the administrative assistant role include providing direct administrative support to the Director of Nursing, supporting the daily operations of the nursing department, coordinating student and faculty health and clinical compliance requirements in collaboration with clinical partners, and providing support to nursing faculty, staff, and students. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Academic Advisor: Actively engage the Catholic Franciscan mission and identity of Marian University by modeling the Franciscan Sponsorship Values and honoring the legacy of the founding congregation through transformative education, unity in diversity leadership through service, integrating faith and life, and institutional policies. Performs all responsibilities in accordance with established policies and procedures of Marian University and the Leighton School of Nursing (LSON) Provides academic advising for pre-nursing and undergraduate nursing students. Presents to students at application sessions and other campus events. Monitors and documents student progress from admission, progression through graduation regarding grades, GPA, degree audits and program requirements. Maintains student files to ensure compliance with the LSON requirements. Communicates concerns about student progress to student, faculty, and the Director of Nursing Other duties as assigned. Administrative Assistant: Actively engage the Catholic Franciscan mission and identity of Marian University by modeling the Franciscan Sponsorship Values, honoring the legacy of the founding congregation, promoting unity in diversity, and integrating the Catholic Franciscan intellectual traditions in courses, programs, and services. Provides administrative support to all members of the MUAC Nursing site as requested including the leadership team, faculty and staff. Supports LSON daily functions including but not limited to the following: Arranges and attends MUAC LSON events including pinning ceremonies as indicated. Facilitates the onboarding and off-boarding of Nursing full time/part time faculty and staff. Arranges requests for building maintenance and IT needs of faculty/staff as requested. Manages accreditation files including hardcopy and electronic files. Maintains LSON files including updates, filing, and purging. Communicates with Nursing faculty/staff on a daily/weekly basis, outcomes of delegated tasks. Manages requests and distribution of office supplies, equipment, and other needs for Nursing faculty/staff. Produces and edits correspondences. Other duties as assigned. University Expectations: Knowledge of and a commitment to the mission of Marian University Adheres to Marian University’s policies and procedures Shows courtesy and respect in interactions with fellow employees, students subordinates, and supervisors Communicates regularly with supervisor about Department issues Meets department productivity standards Participates in developing department goals, objective, and systems Assists to establish department measurements that align and support the accomplishment of the University’s strategic goals Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Excellent organization and communication skills, both written and oral. Ability to advise multiple populations of students simultaneously. Proficient with Microsoft Office suite of products including but not limited to Outlook, Word, Excel, and Power Point. Willingness to learn and become proficient in commonly used office and institutional productively software, student/faculty learning platforms and technology such as Skype, WebEx, etc. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently with minimal guidance and direction. Exhibit professionalism and high ethical standards for maintaining confidential information. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For Consideration All Applications Require: Cover Letter Current resume or CV Contact information of three professional references.  The reference contact information must be entered after the application is submitted in the \"My Presence\" section of the applicant profile. Responses to the supplementary mission & identity questions. Please Review Marian University’s Mission & Identity Statement before responding to the supplementary questions on your application: https://www.marian.edu/faith Essential Functions: Work hours necessary to perform job requirements satisfactorily on a regular basis.  Manage absence from work in responsible manner to ensure service to clients, work teams, and coworkers.  Comply with Marian University policies and practices and seeking clarification of them when necessary. Physical Requirements: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit; use their hands to handle or feel objects, equipment, or controls; and talk or hear. The employee is occasionally required to stand, walk, reach with their hands and arms, climb or balance, and stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 50 pounds.  Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, and the ability to adjust focus. Work Environment: The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Limitations and Disclaimer: The above job description is meant to describe the general nature and level of work being performed; it is not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required for the position. All job requirements are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities.  Some requirements may exclude individuals who pose a direct threat or significant risk to the health and safety of themselves or other employees. This job description in no way states or implies that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee occupying this position.  Employees will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and to perform other job-related duties requested by their supervisor in compliance with Federal and States Laws. Requirements are representative of minimum levels of knowledge, skills and/or abilities.  To perform this job successfully, the employee must possess the abilities or aptitudes to perform each duty proficiently.  Continued employment remains on an “at-will” basis. Marian University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All individuals, including minorities, women, individuals with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws. \nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. Success with Purpose You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
